Files: vendor/*
Copyright: various upstream authors (see the LICENSE/COPYING file shipped in
 each vendor/<name>/ subdirectory)
License: various
Comment: vendor/ bundles source bindings for optional third-party libraries
 Odin programs can build against (SDL2/3, GLFW, raylib, Box2D, Lua, ENet,
 curl, zlib, stb, miniaudio, and others) — none of it Odin's own
 BSD-3-Clause code. Each upstream's own license ships unmodified in place
 (a LICENSE/COPYING file per subdirectory, or a header-comment notice for
 the handful that use that convention instead, e.g. stb, miniaudio). This is
 predominantly permissive (MIT/BSD/zlib-style); a few optional codec
 bindings carry LGPL-family text of their own (vendor/sdl2/mixer,
 vendor/sdl3/mixer, for third-party decoders they wrap). None of it is
 reproduced here — see the files as shipped under
 /usr/lib/amber-odin/vendor/<name>/.

